Subject: web: reject the model groups read instead of answering null

Why: the web shim's generic read fallback answers modelGroups.get() with null;
the renderer stores it as the model group config and the model picker crashes
("界面出错了", Cannot read properties of null (reading 'routes')). The read now
rejects as unsupported, so the renderer keeps its empty defaults.
Upstream: issue and PR drafted in docs/upstream/web-model-groups-null/
(branch fix/web-model-groups-unsupported), not yet submitted.
Remove when: upstream's web shim no longer answers modelGroups.get with null
(either rejected or served by the Host).
diff --git a/apps/host/src/web-shim.test.mjs b/apps/host/src/web-shim.test.mjs
index 8a01f91811..31aa84c568 100644
--- a/apps/host/src/web-shim.test.mjs
+++ b/apps/host/src/web-shim.test.mjs
@@ -223,6 +223,15 @@ test('unsupported web actions cannot report a successful save or execution', asy
   assert.equal(b.calls.length, 0);
 });
 
+// Regression: the generic read fallback answered `modelGroups.get()` with `null`;
+// the renderer stored it as the model group config and the model picker crashed
+// reading `config.routes`. Minimal input: one call, which must reject.
+test('the model groups read rejects instead of answering a null config', async () => {
+  const b = browser();
+  await assert.rejects(b.api.modelGroups.get(), { code: 'HOST_CHANNEL_UNSUPPORTED' });
+  assert.equal(b.calls.length, 0);
+});
+
 // Real-browser regression: opening a task and finishing a reply invoked these
 // desktop presentation hooks without awaiting them, causing unhandled rejections.
 // No native window or notification surface exists in this client; settings writes
